drm: trilinear_dp14: clear the stale AUX interrupt cause before each request

TR_INTERRUPT_CAUSE is a latching, read-to-clear register, and nothing was
clearing it. A REPLY_TIMEOUT left over from an earlier transaction therefore
stayed latched, and the next edp_wait_reply() saw it and declared a timeout
before the new AUX frame had even been sent.

That is not theoretical on this board. Entering Type-C DP Alt Mode resets the
shared SerDes and reliably leaves a timeout latched behind, so the first DPCD
read after a plug fails even though AUX itself is healthy - which in turn
leaves the link policy maker with no sink capabilities to work from.

TR_INTERRUPT_STATE is read-only and does not clear the latch; reading
TR_INTERRUPT_CAUSE is what does. Do that at the top of each request.

Also fix the reply FIFO drain bound while here. The guard read one entry past
the caller's buffer (i <= len instead of i < len) whenever the sink returned
more bytes than were asked for, overrunning the destination by one byte.

Signed-off-by: Paul Goldsmith <goldfish.paul@gmail.com>
---
--- a/bsp/drivers/drm/sunxi_device/hardware/lowlevel_edp/trilinear_dp14/trilinear_dp14.c
+++ b/bsp/drivers/drm/sunxi_device/hardware/lowlevel_edp/trilinear_dp14/trilinear_dp14.c
@@ -458,6 +458,13 @@
 	int i = 0;
 	int cmd;
 
+	/* Clear any stale interrupt cause (e.g. REPLY_TIMEOUT) latched from a
+	 * prior transaction. TR_INTERRUPT_STATE is read-only; reading
+	 * TR_INTERRUPT_CAUSE is what actually clears the latch. Without this,
+	 * edp_wait_reply() can see a false timeout before the next frame
+	 * even starts. */
+	TR_READ(edp_hw, TR_INTERRUPT_CAUSE);
+
 	while (!edp_aux_ready(edp_hw)) {
 		if (count > 5000) {
 			EDP_ERR("last aux reply request timeout, aux request fail now!\n");
@@ -530,7 +537,7 @@
 	case AUX_ACK:
 		for (i = 0; i < request.data_len; i++) {
 			/* add limit to avoid memory exceed */
-			if (i <= len) {
+			if (i < len) {
 				buf[i] = TR_READ(edp_hw, TR_AUX_REPLY_DATA_FIFO);
 				EDP_LOW_DBG("[%s] result: buf[%d] = 0x%x\n", __func__, i, buf[i]);
 			}
@@ -626,7 +633,7 @@
 	switch (reply_code) {
 	case AUX_ACK:
 		for (i = 0; i < request.data_len; i++) {
-			if (i <= len) {
+			if (i < len) {
 				buf[i] = TR_READ(edp_hw, TR_AUX_REPLY_DATA_FIFO);
 				EDP_LOW_DBG("[%s] result: buf[%d] = 0x%x\n", __func__, i, buf[i]);
 			}
